    </p>

    <p>
      <em>Examples:</em>
    </p>

  <exercise workspace="1in">
  <statement>
    <p>
        Flip a coin. Let <m>X = 1</m> if its heads and <m>X=0</m> if its
            tails. Find the pmf of <m>X</m>.
    </p>
  </statement>
  </exercise>
  </page>
  <page>
       <exercise>
  <introduction>
    <p>
        Roll a fair, <m>6-</m> sided die. Let <m>X</m> be the number on top. 
    </p>
  </introduction>
  <task workspace="0.5in">
    <statement>
      <p>
        What is the pmf of <m>X</m>?
      </p>
    </statement>
  </task>
  <task workspace="0.5in">
    <statement>
      <p>
        Find <m>F(3)</m>.
      </p>
    </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>  

    
    <p>
      <alert>Definiton:</alert> If the pmf of <m>X</m> is constant, then
      <m>X</m> is said to have a <fillin characters="25" /> distribution.
    </p>
<exercise>
<introduction>
    <p>
       Suppose <m>X</m> has a uniform distribution on <m>1,2,...,m</m>.
    </p>
</introduction>
<task workspace="1.5in">
<statement>
          <p>
            Find the pmf of <m>X</m>.
          </p>
</statement>
</task>

<task workspace="1.5in">
<statement>
          <p>
            Find the cdf of <m>X</m>.
          </p>
</statement>
</task>
</exercise>
</page>
<page>
<exercise>
<introduction>
    <p>
      Roll a fair, 8=sided die. Let <m>X</m> be the number on top.
    </p>
</introduction>
<task workspace="2.5in">
<statement> <p>
            Find the pmf and cdf of <m>X</m>.
          </p>
</statement>
</task>
<task workspace="0.75in">
<statement>
          <p>
            What is the probability that a <m>2</m> is showing on top?
          </p>
 </statement>
</task>
<task workspace="0.75in">
<statement>
          <p>
            What is the probability that the value is less than 4?
          </p>
    </statement>
</task>
<task workspace="0.75in">
<statement>
          <p>
            What is the probability that the value is at least 2?
          </p>
</statement>
</task>
</exercise>
</page>
<page>

    <p>
      Now let's consider a non-uniform example:
    </p>

    <exercise>
    <introduction>
        <p>
            Suppose there are <m>6</m> winning lottery tickets in a
      stack of <m>50</m>. Draw <m>5</m> at random without replacement. Let
      <m>X</m> be the number of winning lottery tickets.
        </p>
    </introduction>
    <task workspace="0.5in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                What is the space of <m>X</m>?
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1.5in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                Find <m>f(1)=P(X=1)</m>.
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
     <task workspace="1in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            Find the probability that at least one is a winner.
          </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
    </exercise>

<exercise workspace="2in">
<statement>
          <p>
            Draw <m>2</m> cards at random from a standard <m>52</m> card deck.
            Let <m>X</m> be the number of hearts. What is the space of <m>X</m>? Find the pmf of <m>X</m>.
          </p>
</statement>
</exercise>
